In a sandbox web challenge on widget.lab.example, a frame listener processes cross-window messages using a substring check. Why is this origin validation flawed and how is it fixed?

window.addEventListener("message", (ev) => {
  if (ev.origin.includes("lab.example")) updateProfile(ev.data);
});

In a binary security exercise, a C packet parser validates length with a signed integer before calling memcpy. Explain the conversion flaw in this pattern.

int len = read_hdr_len(fd);
if (len > MAX_BUF) return -1;
memcpy(buf, src, len);

A login controller on auth.lab.example restricts redirects to paths starting with a single slash, yet still permits external redirects. Why does this validation fail?

if (nextUrl.startsWith("/")) {
  res.redirect(nextUrl);
}

In a C binary challenge, a slot lookup checks only the upper limit of a signed index before indexing a global .bss array. What memory safety bug results?

static struct item slots[16];
if (idx < 16) return &slots[idx];

In a multithreaded C service lab, two worker threads update a shared packet buffer and its length field without synchronization. How does this data race break bounds checks?

if (shared->len + n <= CAP) {
  shared->len += n;
  memcpy(shared->buf + off, in, n);
}
